1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:12,399
The last government on Earth that could have
stopped him invited him to dinner.

2
00:00:12,968 --> 00:00:18,304
It had taken two years to arrange, through four
intermediaries, and the terms had been

3
00:00:18,324 --> 00:00:23,909
negotiated with the seriousness of an arms control
treaty. He would come without security.

4
00:00:23,929 --> 00:00:29,451
There would be no announcement, before or after.
There would be no photographs. And there

5
00:00:29,471 --> 00:00:34,744
would be one other person at the table, who would
not be named in any record, because

6
00:00:34,764 --> 00:00:40,225
she did not officially exist in any capacity that
would permit her to sit at that table.

7
00:00:40,795 --> 00:00:46,495
Wen Shulan was seventy-one. She had been a deputy
minister of state security for eleven

8
00:00:46,515 --> 00:00:52,083
years and then something without a title for eight
more, and she had spent twenty-two

9
00:00:52,103 --> 00:00:57,079
years, on and off, reading everything there was
to read about Albert Wesker.

10
00:00:57,649 --> 00:01:02,477
She had been right about him before anyone else on
Earth, and she had never once been

11
00:01:02,497 --> 00:01:06,242
able to say so in a sentence that would
not have ended her career.

12
00:01:08,311 --> 00:01:14,235
The third person at the table was a member of the
Politburo Standing Committee whose name

13
00:01:14,255 --> 00:01:20,179
does not matter to this story, and who said perhaps
forty words all evening, and listened

14
00:01:20,199 --> 00:01:21,849
to every one of the rest.

15
00:01:24,039 --> 00:01:26,145
You have taken eleven countries.

16
00:01:26,665 --> 00:01:32,850
Association agreements with two states and nine
provinces. Nobody's flag has changed.

17
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:38,759
Doctor Wesker. We are three people in a room with no
recording. Let us not waste the evening.

18
00:01:40,278 --> 00:01:43,694
Fourteen, then. There are three more that
haven't been announced.

19
00:01:45,713 --> 00:01:51,768
The Standing Committee member did not look up from his
soup. Wen Shulan smiled — the second

20
00:01:51,788 --> 00:01:55,507
smile anyone at the Ministry had ever
recorded from her.

21
00:01:56,197 --> 00:01:57,222
Thank you.

22
00:01:59,742 --> 00:02:05,062
What followed was the most consequential
conversation of the twenty-first century, and

23
00:02:05,082 --> 00:02:06,242
the least dramatic.

24
00:02:06,811 --> 00:02:13,064
There was no threat. Both sides had worked out,
years before, exactly what threats were

25
00:02:13,084 --> 00:02:19,410
available and exactly why none of them worked. China
could not embargo Umbrella; a fifth

26
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:25,682
of its own pharmaceutical supply and most of its
vaccine capacity ran through the joint

27
00:02:25,702 --> 00:02:32,388
venture in Singapore. Umbrella could not coerce China;
China made forty percent of everything

28
00:02:32,408 --> 00:02:38,877
Umbrella's factories assembled, and had done for a
generation, and had spent fifteen years

29
00:02:38,897 --> 00:02:41,833
quietly ensuring that this remained true.

30
00:02:42,403 --> 00:02:48,336
They were not enemies. They were the only two
structures left on Earth of comparable weight,

31
00:02:48,356 --> 00:02:53,900
and they both knew it, and the entire evening was
about establishing, precisely, where

32
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:54,741
the line ran.

33
00:02:56,932 --> 00:02:59,005
You will not take our provinces.

34
00:02:59,526 --> 00:03:00,145
No.

35
00:03:00,665 --> 00:03:03,883
You will not take the provinces of our
neighbours who look to us.

36
00:03:04,403 --> 00:03:06,296
That's a longer list than the first one.

37
00:03:06,817 --> 00:03:07,887
It is.

38
00:03:09,407 --> 00:03:15,435
Then let's write it down. Not as a treaty — neither
of us can sign a treaty. As a map,

39
00:03:15,455 --> 00:03:19,936
with names on it, which neither of us
will ever show to anybody.

40
00:03:21,956 --> 00:03:27,927
They spent four hours on the map. It was the only
physical object produced that evening,

41
00:03:27,947 --> 00:03:33,782
and there were two copies, and both of them still
exist, and one of them is in a vault

42
00:03:33,802 --> 00:03:37,935
under a mountain outside Beijing, and
the other is on Arklay.

43
00:03:38,504 --> 00:03:44,800
It divided the surface of the Earth into three parts:
what was China's, what was Umbrella's,

44
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:49,331
and what was neither — which, in twenty
forty-six, was most of it.

45
00:03:51,901 --> 00:03:57,829
It held for nineteen years. That is a very long
time, for a line drawn on a map by two

46
00:03:57,849 --> 00:04:00,527
people who had no authority to draw it.

47
00:04:02,597 --> 00:04:08,452
At eleven o'clock the Standing Committee member
thanked them both, and left, and did not

48
00:04:08,472 --> 00:04:11,056
come back. That had also been arranged.

49
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:14,126
Wen Shulan poured the last of the tea.

50
00:04:14,816 --> 00:04:17,458
May I ask you something that is
not business?

51
00:04:17,978 --> 00:04:18,891
You've earned one.

52
00:04:19,411 --> 00:04:24,893
Twenty-two years ago I watched a recording of you
sitting in silence on an American television

53
00:04:24,913 --> 00:04:29,869
programme, and I recognised the rhythm of it. I
have never been able to say to anyone

54
00:04:29,889 --> 00:04:34,845
what I recognised, because it is not sayable. But I
would like to say it once, aloud,

55
00:04:34,865 --> 00:04:37,363
to you, and then I will never
say it again.

56
00:04:39,762 --> 00:04:44,559
My grandfather was in Nanjing in nineteen
thirty-seven. He was nine years old. He did

57
00:04:44,579 --> 00:04:49,433
not talk about it for fifty years, and then he
talked about it for one evening, when I

58
00:04:49,453 --> 00:04:52,776
was a grown woman, and then he never
talked about it again.

59
00:04:54,675 --> 00:04:59,504
When I listen to you speak, Doctor Wesker, I hear
the cadence of the men who did that

60
00:04:59,524 --> 00:05:04,353
to my grandfather's city. Not the language. The
shape. The pause before the important

61
00:05:04,373 --> 00:05:08,403
word. The way a sentence is built so that a
crowd will breathe with it.

62
00:05:10,303 --> 00:05:15,091
I do not know what you are. I have stopped trying
to know. But I know that shape, and

63
00:05:15,111 --> 00:05:20,124
I want you to understand that one person on this
planet hears it every time you open your

64
00:05:20,144 --> 00:05:20,463
mouth.

65
00:05:23,483 --> 00:05:26,297
In the quiet of one skull, nothing moved.

66
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:33,111
The Adolf half of the mind — which had spent twenty
years being described, in a hundred

67
00:05:33,131 --> 00:05:39,591
ways, by people who had no idea it was there — heard
itself identified, accurately, across

68
00:05:39,611 --> 00:05:42,903
a dinner table, by an old woman
with a teapot.

69
00:05:43,473 --> 00:05:49,777
And the Wesker half felt the thing it had felt exactly
twice before: at a dinner in Philadelphia,

70
00:05:49,797 --> 00:05:55,385
when a journalist had asked about Control Seven, and
in a doorway, on the first night,

71
00:05:55,405 --> 00:05:58,841
when an old security guard had said
different animal.

72
00:06:01,031 --> 00:06:04,936
And knowing that, you've just spent four
hours drawing a map with me.

73
00:06:05,456 --> 00:06:06,337
Yes.

74
00:06:06,857 --> 00:06:07,434
Why?

75
00:06:09,954 --> 00:06:14,926
Because my grandfather's city was destroyed by men
who could not be stopped and were not

76
00:06:14,946 --> 00:06:19,748
managed. Nobody tried to manage them. They tried to
appease them, and then they tried

77
00:06:19,768 --> 00:06:24,684
to fight them, and both were catastrophes, and my
grandfather was nine years old in the

78
00:06:24,704 --> 00:06:25,422
middle of it.

79
00:06:26,822 --> 00:06:31,496
I cannot stop you. I have known that for nineteen
years, and I have written it in four

80
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:36,299
assessments, each of which was read by fewer people
than the last. So I will manage you.

81
00:06:36,319 --> 00:06:41,048
For as long as I am alive, and then I will hand the
file to someone else, with the map,

82
00:06:41,068 --> 00:06:42,631
and they will manage you too.

83
00:06:44,531 --> 00:06:50,013
That is the entire policy of the People's Republic of
China toward Albert Wesker. I wrote

84
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:53,846
it. It is one sentence long, and it is:
keep him at the table.

85
00:06:56,865 --> 00:06:58,754
He looked at her for a long time.

86
00:06:59,444 --> 00:07:03,026
That's the best policy anyone on this
planet has about me.

87
00:07:03,545 --> 00:07:06,707
I know. It is also the only one
that has ever worked.

88
00:07:09,226 --> 00:07:11,391
One government did not draw a map.

89
00:07:11,961 --> 00:07:17,829
Colonel Arkady Belov was sixty-nine years old and
had been retired twice, and had both

90
00:07:17,849 --> 00:07:23,716
times been brought back, because there was no one
else in the Federal Security Service

91
00:07:23,736 --> 00:07:28,987
who had spent sixteen years on a single file
and could recite it from memory.

92
00:07:29,557 --> 00:07:35,468
He had never been promoted past colonel. That was
deliberate; colonels can be disowned.

93
00:07:35,488 --> 00:07:41,330
He had an office with a window, a photograph of
twelve men on his desk, and the quiet,

94
00:07:41,350 --> 00:07:47,124
complete support of exactly four people in the
Russian state, none of whom would ever

95
00:07:47,144 --> 00:07:48,759
put anything in writing.

96
00:07:50,829 --> 00:07:56,114
He had told their mothers about Mali himself, in
their kitchens, in twenty thirty. He

97
00:07:56,134 --> 00:08:01,420
had been lying, and he had known he was lying, and
three of them had known it too and

98
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,607
had let him finish.

99
00:08:03,177 --> 00:08:09,406
In twenty forty-six, the arithmetic finally arrived
at a number he could use. Umbrella's

100
00:08:09,425 --> 00:08:15,583
Territory sat in the middle of the Atlantic, four
kilometres across, with a hundred and

101
00:08:15,603 --> 00:08:22,115
sixty thousand people on it and no air defence that
anyone could identify, because a private

102
00:08:22,134 --> 00:08:25,097
corporation could not legally possess one.

103
00:08:25,786 --> 00:08:30,822
It is a city on a raft. And he is on it
two hundred days a year.

104
00:08:33,342 --> 00:08:39,291
The order that went to the submarine was not a Russian
state order. This has been established,

105
00:08:39,311 --> 00:08:45,069
as far as anything is ever established, by three
separate inquiries. It came from a colonel

106
00:08:45,089 --> 00:08:50,847
with four friends and a photograph on his desk,
through a chain of people who each believed

107
00:08:50,867 --> 00:08:55,482
it came from someone above them, and it took
nineteen months to assemble.

108
00:08:56,052 --> 00:09:01,909
What left the water off the Norwegian coast at four
in the morning on the nineteenth of

109
00:09:01,929 --> 00:09:07,786
November was a single ballistic missile with a
conventional warhead — a very large one,

110
00:09:07,806 --> 00:09:13,798
of the kind designed for hardened bunkers — on a
ballistic profile that would put it into

111
00:09:13,818 --> 00:09:18,054
the Atlantic, on Arklay Free Territory,
eighteen minutes later.

112
00:09:22,123 --> 00:09:28,219
Eleven governments saw it launch. Four of them had,
by then, standing instructions about

113
00:09:28,239 --> 00:09:34,474
what to do if anything was ever launched at Arklay,
and all four did the same thing, which

114
00:09:34,494 --> 00:09:36,281
was to telephone Umbrella.

115
00:09:36,851 --> 00:09:40,371
They need not have bothered. Umbrella
had seen it first.

116
00:09:43,191 --> 00:09:46,407
Purchase confirmed. Aegis lattice.

117
00:09:49,791 --> 00:09:55,389
He had bought it fourteen months before, after the
second attempt on his life, and it

118
00:09:55,409 --> 00:10:01,271
had sat in orbit doing nothing, in four hundred and
eleven pieces that every space agency

119
00:10:01,291 --> 00:10:05,832
on Earth had catalogued as a commercial
communications constellation.

120
00:10:06,402 --> 00:10:09,142
It was not a communications constellation.

121
00:10:11,211 --> 00:10:17,186
The intercept happened at an altitude of three hundred
and ten kilometres, over the Denmark

122
00:10:17,206 --> 00:10:20,611
Strait, nine minutes and forty
seconds after launch.

123
00:10:21,182 --> 00:10:26,708
A hundred and sixty thousand people on Arklay Free
Territory saw a silent white flash,

124
00:10:26,728 --> 00:10:32,255
very high up and very far to the north, like a star
that came on for a second and then

125
00:10:32,275 --> 00:10:38,059
went out. Most of them thought it was a meteor. The
ones on the night shift in the harbour

126
00:10:38,079 --> 00:10:44,057
took photographs of it, which went online within the
hour, and which Tomás Reyes's department

127
00:10:44,077 --> 00:10:48,959
did not suppress, because there was nothing to
suppress: a light in the sky.

128
00:10:51,528 --> 00:10:57,540
The Director was awake. He had been awake since the
launch, nine minutes and forty seconds

129
00:10:57,560 --> 00:11:03,571
of which he had spent in the Thought Acceleration,
which is a subjective ninety-six hours,

130
00:11:03,591 --> 00:11:07,458
most of which he had spent deciding
what to do afterwards.

131
00:11:08,028 --> 00:11:10,348
What he decided was: nothing.

132
00:11:12,538 --> 00:11:13,499
Nothing.

133
00:11:14,019 --> 00:11:19,625
Nothing public. No statement, no accusation, no
retaliation, no demand. Somebody fired

134
00:11:19,645 --> 00:11:25,186
a bunker-buster at a civilian city of a hundred and
sixty thousand people and a light

135
00:11:25,206 --> 00:11:31,336
came on in the sky for one second and went out. That is
the entire story. Let every government

136
00:11:31,356 --> 00:11:36,898
on Earth work out for themselves what just
happened, and let every one of them arrive

137
00:11:36,918 --> 00:11:42,590
at the same conclusion in private, and let none of
them ever be able to say it out loud

138
00:11:42,610 --> 00:11:45,337
without admitting that they were watching.

139
00:11:45,857 --> 00:11:50,252
You are teaching them a lesson that
has no words in it.

140
00:11:50,773 --> 00:11:52,749
Those are the only lessons that last.

141
00:11:55,269 --> 00:12:01,112
Nineteen governments understood, between four and six
o'clock that morning, that Umbrella

142
00:12:01,132 --> 00:12:06,844
Life Sciences had a functioning global ballistic
missile defence system, which no state

143
00:12:06,864 --> 00:12:10,731
on Earth possessed, and which it had
chosen not to mention.

144
00:12:11,302 --> 00:12:16,785
The word for what that made Umbrella is not a
corporate word. Every foreign ministry on

145
00:12:16,805 --> 00:12:21,656
the planet found the correct word within a
week, and none of them printed it.

146
00:12:24,225 --> 00:12:29,913
Arkady Belov was not arrested. That would have
required a record of the order.

147
00:12:30,485 --> 00:12:36,474
He was retired for the third time, in January of
twenty forty-seven, with a pension and

148
00:12:36,494 --> 00:12:42,414
a medal for long service, and he went to a house
outside Tver that had belonged to his

149
00:12:42,434 --> 00:12:46,145
wife's family, and he lived there
for four more years.

150
00:12:46,715 --> 00:12:52,972
He was found, in twenty fifty-one, in the chair by
the window. The photograph of twelve

151
00:12:52,992 --> 00:12:59,105
men was on the table beside him. The inquiry into
his death, such as it was, recorded

152
00:12:59,125 --> 00:13:05,383
natural causes, and nobody in any of four
intelligence services believed it, and nobody

153
00:13:05,403 --> 00:13:10,289
in any of four intelligence services asked
a second question either.

154
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:18,296
The Director did not order it. That is worth saying
plainly, because by twenty fifty-one

155
00:13:18,316 --> 00:13:21,892
it had stopped being the kind of thing
he needed to order.

156
00:13:22,461 --> 00:13:28,020
Somewhere in an organisation of four hundred and
eighty thousand people, some of whom

157
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:33,599
were not people, somebody had worked out what would
be useful. That is what an empire

158
00:13:33,619 --> 00:13:39,308
is. It is the point at which the will at the top no
longer has to be expressed, because

159
00:13:39,328 --> 00:13:40,884
it has been distributed.

160
00:13:44,453 --> 00:13:50,168
He walked back to the guest house. It was three
kilometres, and it was cold, and he had

161
00:13:50,188 --> 00:13:53,793
no security, and nobody in Beijing
looked at him twice.

162
00:13:55,484 --> 00:13:56,707
She named us.

163
00:13:57,226 --> 00:13:58,187
She named you.

164
00:13:58,707 --> 00:14:06,269
She named the shape of a sentence. It is the same
thing. I built that shape in beer halls

165
00:14:06,289 --> 00:14:11,125
when the men who built the first
radios were still alive.

166
00:14:13,024 --> 00:14:14,504
Does it trouble you?

167
00:14:15,024 --> 00:14:16,679
No. That's what troubles me.

168
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,592
He walked for a while.

169
00:14:21,282 --> 00:14:25,995
Twenty years ago it would have. Twenty years ago
I'd have spent the night working out

170
00:14:26,015 --> 00:14:30,841
how to remove her. And tonight I sat at a table with
a woman who has heard exactly what

171
00:14:30,861 --> 00:14:35,686
is inside my head, and I drew a map with her, and
I'm walking home in the cold thinking

172
00:14:35,706 --> 00:14:40,587
that she is the best adversary I will ever have and
that I would like her to live a long

173
00:14:40,607 --> 00:14:40,865
time.

174
00:14:41,385 --> 00:14:42,688
You have grown.

175
00:14:43,208 --> 00:14:47,433
I've grown comfortable. It's not the same
thing, and it's more dangerous.

176
00:14:49,953 --> 00:14:55,087
He stopped under a lantern and looked at his own
reflection in a closed shop window.

177
00:14:55,658 --> 00:14:58,846
Ninety-seven percent. Zero divergences.

178
00:14:59,417 --> 00:15:05,152
He had stopped arguing with the voice in his head, and
he had told himself that this meant

179
00:15:05,172 --> 00:15:10,587
he had won the argument. Standing in a cold street
in Beijing at midnight, he allowed

180
00:15:10,607 --> 00:15:14,871
himself, for about four seconds, to
consider the other possibility.

181
00:15:15,442 --> 00:15:16,688
Then he walked on.
